<title>UK: Berkeley unit sells portfolio of properties.</title>
<headline>Berkeley unit sells portfolio of properties.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Berkeley Group Plc said on Thursday its associated company Berkeley Eastoak Investments Ltd has disposed of a portfolio of commercial investment properties.</p>
<p>It was sold for a total cash consideration of 103 million stg, representing an initial yield of 7.6 percent, to a leading UK Life Fund following an unsolicited offer.</p>
<p>The profit to the group is approximately 5.5 million stg before tax, Berkeley group said in a statement.</p>
<p>The portfolio comprised 23 properties consisting of retail warehouse parks, leisure properties, and industrial warehouses and offices.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
